From 7197a996495e4cf9b83da49b5fc0c9fda528a287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:00:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/59] m3 particles: material cut-out, per-layer UV source

- particle.frag: u_alphaTest; mask alpha below the material threshold is
  discarded, as in standard.frag. Helios debris drew as rectangles.
- Vertex buffer gains the whole-quad UV (stride 11). particle.vert puts
  the quad UV on coordinates 0 to 2 and the flipbook cell on 3.
- particlerender binds a layer with uvSource 6 (particle flipbook) to the
  cell; every other layer reads the whole quad (WhiteoutFlakes
  m3_surface_table). Blimp steam drew as soft rectangles.
- Displacement particles share the buffer layout and the UV rule.

Known defects:
- Light shaft emitters still re-burst on each loop (next change).
